---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie policy"
  description="The current site avoids non-essential cookies and documents what must change before analytics is connected."
  path="/cookies/"
  updated="24 Aug 2026"
>
  <h2>Current position</h2>
  <p>
    This build does not install third-party analytics, advertising pixels, session-replay tools or
    other non-essential cookie technology. The contact form can capture campaign parameters in
    hidden fields, but does not store them in a browser cookie.
  </p>

  <h2>Essential browser storage</h2>
  <p>
    The current static interface does not intentionally create essential cookies. Infrastructure
    providers may process ordinary request metadata needed to deliver and protect the site; their
    production configuration must be reviewed before this draft is approved.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics events</h2>
  <p>
    The site emits a small event layer for primary CTA clicks, methodology links, form start,
    confirmed form success, template downloads, FAQ expansion, benchmark views and outbound contact
    actions. These events remain in the page unless an approved analytics provider is connected.
  </p>

  <h2>Future changes</h2>
  <p>
    Before adding a provider, DataDecision should document the provider, identifiers, retention,
    purposes, legal basis and consent behavior. If non-essential cookies are introduced, the consent
    interface and this policy must be updated before the tracking code is enabled.
  </p>

  <h2>Your control</h2>
  <p>
    Because this build does not install non-essential cookies, there is no cosmetic consent banner.
    A future banner should appear only if the deployed technology and applicable rules require a
    real choice.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
